    <string name="preset_usage_neutral">No coloration: a clean reference, or the base for a headphone correction on its own.</string>
    <string name="preset_usage_very_strong">Very strong boost: for loud listening on speakers that can take it. If it booms or pumps, lower Punch or Bass first.</string>
    <string name="preset_usage_kick">Kick-focused low end: punchy at high volume, and it booms less in a car, where the cabin already adds sub bass.</string>
    <string name="preset_usage_sub">Deep sub bass: for headphones and systems that reach down to 40 Hz. Can boom in a car.</string>
    <string name="preset_usage_quiet">Loudness compensation: made for low volume, such as a quiet drive at night.</string>
    <string name="preset_usage_small_drivers">Virtual bass: for in-ears and small speakers. Works in the built-in player only.</string>
    <string name="preset_usage_softened_highs">Softened upper mids: for harsh, heavily distorted tracks or bright earbuds.</string>
    <string name="preset_usage_all_rounder">A moderate all-rounder: fits most headphones and speakers.</string>
    <string name="preset_usage_strongest">Strongest boost: +%1$.1f dB. The built-in player lowers everything else by that much, so turn the volume up a little.</string>
